    </thead><tbody>
    <tr>
     <td colspan="2"><para unique="1091404">66 0F 38 40 /r</para>
      <para unique="1091405">PMULLD xmm1, xmm2/m128</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1091409">A</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1091411">V/V</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1091413">SSE4_1</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1091415">Multiply the packed dword signed integers in xmm1 and xmm2/m128 and store the low 32 bits of each product in xmm1.</para>
      </td>
     </tr>
    <tr>
     <td colspan="2"><para unique="1091417">VEX.128.66.0F38.WIG 40 /r</para>
      <para unique="1091418">VPMULLD xmm1, xmm2, xmm3/m128</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1091422">B</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1091424">V/V</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1091426">AVX</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1091428">Multiply the packed dword signed integers in xmm2 and xmm3/m128 and store the low 32 bits of each product in xmm1.</para>
      </td>
     </tr>
    <tr>
     <td colspan="2"><para unique="1091430">VEX.256.66.0F38.WIG 40 /r</para>
      <para unique="1091431">VPMULLD ymm1, ymm2, ymm3/m256</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1091435">B</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1091437">V/V</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1091439">AVX2</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1091441">Multiply the packed dword signed integers in ymm2 and ymm3/m256 and store the low 32 bits of each product in ymm1.</para>
      </td>
     </tr>
    <tr>
     <td colspan="2"><para unique="1092105">EVEX.128.66.0F38.W0 40 /r</para>
      <para unique="1092106">VPMULLD xmm1 {k1}{z}, xmm2, xmm3/m128/m32bcst</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1092110">C</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1092112">V/V</para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1092114">(AVX512VL AND</para>
      <para unique="1092118">AVX512F) OR AVX10.1<anchor id="+570234"/></para>
      </td>
     <td><para unique="1092123">Multiply the packed dword signed integers in xmm2 and xmm3/m128/m32bcst and store the low 32 bits of each product in xmm1 under writemask k1.</para>
      </td>
     </tr>
    <tr>
     <td colspan="2"><para unique="1092088">EVEX.256.66.0F38.W0 40 /r</para>
      <para unique="1092089">VPMULLD ymm1 {k1}{z}, ymm2, ymm3/m256/m32bcst</para>
